      "writtenOn": "2020-10-01T16:48:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, producing and using an integer-typed bit mask with an enum as one of the inputs is totally valid. Assigning an unenumerated value to an enum-typed variable, e.g. a function argument, could produce an out-of-range assignment, if the value is outside the range of the underlying enum type. However, if the value is a bitwise OR of enumerated values, that isn\u0027t possible. That\u0027s why I\u0027m generally comfortable with using enums to define bit fields. This is a nit, though.",
